[00:17.30] She drinks the life-blood from the feebled man
[00:22.66] Empty bodies, soul-drained by the virgin queen
[00:27.26] Finally given the pleasure to die
[00:41.13] She aligns the hate inside their hearts
[00:46.24] Her chosen knights will make sure all life departs
[00:51.44] Soon comes the end of all, she watched a chamber fall
[00:56.92] She heard her master call
[01:00.57] Live my words, oh, sacred child, you're soon to leave this world defiled
[01:05.98] Then what awaits me my lord?
[01:09.10] Trust me my child, your wishes shall not be ignored
[01:12.94] And then he spoke his mind, now his will is hers
[01:15.70] The earth shall fall, the eternal curse is cast on the sands they walk
[01:21.98] 
[02:24.17] Now you must use your power, show the human race you are the one
[02:29.56] Use their trust forever and then deceive their weakened minds
[02:36.17] Fool them to destroy themselves in hopelessness
[02:41.57] Belie their seeds, belie their dreams, all hope has ceased to be
[02:57.83] The people worshipped their queen
[03:00.60] Such beauty before her time was unseen
[03:04.03] They were fooled by her presence and disguise
[03:09.40] Faithfully, they listened and swallowed all her lies
[03:14.72] The times are changing, rearranging the patterns of our lives
[03:22.13] So let your heart stop beating beneath this twisted sky
[03:33.34] They were embraced by sadness, but not afraid to die
[03:42.69] 
[04:14.74] So pass this sacred dagger and let yourself fly free
[04:40.01] So pretend that you are dreaming and rise above this world of you and me
[05:02.46] Liar!
[05:05.28] All those who died with you by their side were denied access to the higher ground
[05:12.76] Betrayal!
[05:15.79] Eternal detest from the ones left unblessed, so possessed
[05:19.37] Their last caress was your knife in their hearts
[05:33.45] Fed from her deed, watching them bleed
[05:38.38] In her own conceit, a world to delete, lies at her feet
[05:43.44] Her demon inside do no longer hide
[05:48.72] Showing its face of hate and disgrace leaving their saviour unpraised
[05:54.72] 